# rk3588.env — pipeline environment on the RK3588 car computer (Orange Pi 5 Plus).
# Installed to /etc/dv/rk3588.env by rk3588_tuning.sh and loaded by the dv-pipeline
# drop-in it installs. Measured layout: docs/arm_optimization/validation.md (level 5).
#
# Core pinning: the per-scan pipeline gets the A76 cores, one process per core:
#   A76  4 detection · 5 SLAM · 6 planning · 7 control + odometry filter + NIC interrupts
# Everything else (mode manager, mission control, watchdog, sim supervisor, LiDAR driver,
# recorder, viewer bridge, static TFs) floats on the A55 cores 0-3, where the drop-in
# starts the launch. Pinning those to one A55 each lost more scans in the HIL A/B
# (validation.md, level 5), so they stay unpinned.
# Quoted: systemd and bash (the HIL start script sources it) both read it whole.
# Control moved from 6 to 7: planning and control together held core 6 at ~99 % while
# core 7 sat at ~27 % (HIL, c488839), and each slowed the other.
DV_CPU_PIN="cone_detection_node=4 slam_node=5 path_planning_node=6 control_node=7 odometry_filter_node=7"
# One thread per numeric library: the parallelism comes from the pinned processes.
# More threads on a pinned core only time-slice against each other.
OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1
OMP_NUM_THREADS=1
MKL_NUM_THREADS=1
NUMBA_NUM_THREADS=1
